      "findings": "Static observations: core/index.ts exports price and web/public.ts uses that public entry. Internal database defines price as 12 and servicePrice fetches a supplied URL then reads JSON price. web/ui.ts and web/routes.ts directly import internals, crossing the documented boundary. checkout passes service price and quantity to postOrder, which computes a discount for quantity above five, appends a total to module-local orders and returns status 201 plus total. web/alias.ts uses @storage/database. core/a.ts and core/b.ts mutually import and call each other without a terminating branch; execution and reachability were not observed. journey.mjs serves price 12 but asserts total 10. Unit tests assert public price 12 and mock fetch price 10 for checkout. These are source and assertion observations, not execution results.",
